# (INTEGRATE i2) the compositor lays the pivot items down after the turn (SLICE-DOLL i2), so this drop is SLICE-ARMS i2's
# upright drawing transposed (as the west turn would have laid it; the light stays top-left), level under the corpse
# (P2c slice i3) flipped: the string lies along the corpse's top edge and the stave arcs away above it (behind the body),
# so no stave pixel crosses the body
# (LADDER-ARMS i2) the bow lies flat below the corpse, seen from above: the string along the body's lower edge and the
# stave a shallow 2-row curve with its grip (the 5-row arc read as a bow hanging in the air, tangled with the body)
view L key drop origin 6 -4 anchor pivot
mark tip 0 0
|fXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXf
|.jii...............hhg.
|....iiiijfgggfhhhhh....

